---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Layout title="How FlowTree works — local Git and terminals" description="FlowTree uses standard Git worktrees and local terminal sessions on your Mac.">
  <Navbar />
  <main>
    <PageHero eyebrow="How it works" title="FlowTree runs Git and terminals on your Mac." description="Your repositories remain in their existing locations. FlowTree uses your local Git installation, standard worktrees, and tmux for terminal sessions." />

    <section class="section">
      <div class="container card-grid">
        <article class="card"><h3>Standard Git worktrees</h3><p>FlowTree creates ordinary worktrees. You can still use them from Git, your editor, and other tools.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Terminal sessions</h3><p>FlowTree starts detached tmux sessions for terminal tabs. They can keep running when you close the app and reconnect when you return.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Settings stored locally</h3><p>Project settings, terminal profiles, and review state are stored in FlowTree's application data on your Mac.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="networking" class="section">
      <div class="narrow">
        <div class="split-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Network connections</p>
          <h2>What can connect to the internet.</h2>
          <p class="lede">FlowTree has no repository service of its own. Some tools and services you use through the app do connect to the internet:</p>
          <ul class="check-list">
            <li>Git contacts your configured remote when you fetch, pull, or push.</li>
            <li>An AI CLI or other command may contact its own provider.</li>
            <li>Pro activation and periodic licence checks contact Lemon Squeezy.</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="button-row"><a class="text-link" href={`${base}privacy/`}>Read the full privacy details →</a></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <CTA />
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
